# MQTT Broker Configuration
# ==========================
# Copy this file to .env.mqtt and fill in your broker credentials.
# The .env.mqtt file is gitignored and will NOT be committed.
#
# Configuration priority:
#   1. Environment variables (highest)
#   2. .env.mqtt file values
#   3. Built-in defaults (topics only)
#
# For HiveMQ Cloud:
#   - Sign up at https://www.hivemq.com/cloud/
#   - Create a cluster and note the hostname
#   - Create credentials under "Access Management"
#   - Port 8883 is the standard TLS MQTT port
#
# For other brokers:
#   - Use the broker's hostname, port, and credentials
#   - Set MQTT_USE_TLS=false only for local/trusted brokers

# Required — no defaults
MQTT_BROKER_HOST=your-cluster-id.s1.eu.hivemq.cloud
MQTT_USERNAME=your_mqtt_username
MQTT_PASSWORD=your_mqtt_password

# Optional — shown with defaults
MQTT_BROKER_PORT=8883
MQTT_CLIENT_ID=face_robot_laptop
MQTT_USE_TLS=true

# MQTT topics — shown with defaults
MQTT_TOPIC_COMMAND=robot/face_following/command
MQTT_TOPIC_STATUS=robot/face_following/status
MQTT_TOPIC_TELEMETRY=robot/face_following/telemetry
